# STATE FILES
# Do NOT create new .a2ml files. The format is being retired estate-wide in
# favour of repo-deed clauses (rsr-template-repo#209); the .a2ml files already in
# .machine_readable/ are the historical record and retire with the deed, not
# before it. Never "fix" a missing file by adding a root duplicate — this repo
# paid for that habit twice (SECURITY.md + SECURITY.adoc, MAINTAINERS +
# MAINTAINERS.adoc).

# CI / SUPPLY CHAIN — read before touching .github/
# Every `uses:` ref in a workflow must be SHA-pinned AND recorded in
# .github/workflows/actions.lock, transitively closed. GitHub refuses a run
# whose refs the lockfile does not record: zero jobs, no log. Dependabot cannot
# regenerate the lockfile, so a Dependabot workflow bump needs a matching lock
# refresh in the same change. Regenerate with standards'
# scripts/update-actions-lock.sh; verify locally with scripts/check-lock-sync.sh
# (`just check-lock-sync`). Do not hand-edit actions.lock.

# BANNED PATTERNS (Rust)
# transmute — except at an FFI boundary with a `// SAFETY:` comment.
# Also avoid: unwrap in library code paths that can see user input, unsafe
# blocks without a safety comment, assert_total-style totality cheats in
# dependent-type proofs.

# BANNED LANGUAGES (for NEW files; standards/3-practice/LANGUAGE-POLICY.adoc)
# Go -> Rust.  Python -> Julia or Rust.  TypeScript/ReScript/Deno -> do not add;
# JavaScript only via Bun (package.json + bun.lock).

# CONTAINERS
# Runtime: Podman first. File: Containerfile (never Dockerfile).
# Base: cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base:latest or cgr.dev/chainguard/static:latest.
# This repo ships no container today; `?container/` stays off the allowlist
# until one exists.

# BUILD
# Use `just` (Justfile) for all tasks: `just --list`. `just all` is fmt + check
# + build + test; `just verify` is the no-toolchain gate set.

# STYLE
# Descriptive names. Document all files. AsciiDoc for prose (docs/ holds no .md
# files). Every claim about what is implemented must be checkable — see
# docs/AFFIRMATION.adoc for the pattern, and do not restate a claim the tests do
# not support.
